================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY CREDITS AND LICENCE COMPATIBILITY
================================================================================

ClickStorm contains no third-party source code. Every file in this repository
is original work by the copyright holder above, so the MIT licence above is
the only licence that applies to the distributed program.

The projects below were read while designing the click engine. Their
measurements, behaviour and design ideas informed decisions; where a licence
would not have allowed reuse, nothing was copied at all. This section records
that credit and the licence check so the project's licensing stays auditable.

Verified 2026-11-25 against each project's repository:

  Project                Licence        Compatible with MIT?  What was used
  ---------------------  -------------  --------------------  --------------
  chris101-dev/          MIT            Yes                   Drift-free pacing
  ColibriTap                                                against an absolute
                                                            deadline on a
                                                            monotonic clock.

  PriyanshuGeTRekT/      MIT            Yes                   Posting button
  WinClicker                                                messages straight to
                                                            a window for
                                                            background clicks
                                                            (the "Direct"
                                                            delivery mode).

  local764larp/          None declared  No - all rights       Published
  auto-clicker           ("not yet      reserved              delivered-vs-
                          chosen")                            emitted CPS
                                                            measurements and
                                                            the timer / yield /
                                                            spin wait tiers.
                                                            No code used.

  Blur009/               GPL-3.0        No - copyleft,        Feature ideas only
  Blur-AutoClicker                      incompatible with     (click and time
                                        an MIT release)       limits, position
                                                              clicking). No code
                                                              used, because
                                                              GPL-3.0 code cannot
                                                              be relicensed under
                                                              MIT.

  Assassin654/           GPL-2.0        No - copyleft,        Background
  AutoClicker                           incompatible with     "ghost click"
                                        an MIT release        behaviour: button
                                                              messages sent
                                                              synchronously to a
                                                              window. No code
                                                              used; SYNC is an
                                                              independent
                                                              SendMessageTimeout
                                                              design.

Summary of the compatibility check:

  * MIT-licensed projects (ColibriTap, WinClicker): compatible in both
    directions. Their notices are honoured by the credit above.
  * Projects with no licence (local764larp/auto-clicker): not reusable. Only
    published numbers and ideas were taken, which does not copy the work.
  * GPL-3.0 projects (Blur Auto Clicker) and GPL-2.0 projects (Paul's
    AutoClicker): not compatible with an MIT distribution. No code was taken;
    only non-copyrightable behaviour and measurements were used. ClickStorm's
    SYNC mode is an independent SendMessageTimeout implementation of the
    synchronous-message idea, not a translation of that project.

Deliberately not used: kernel-mode input drivers such as Interception
(https://github.com/oblitum/Interception). They would add an
administrator-installed signed driver dependency and change this project's
licensing and distribution story, so ClickStorm stays user-mode only.

If you believe something here is credited incorrectly, open an issue and it
will be corrected or removed.
